---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const eirs = [
    {
        name: 'Katherine Katcher',
        project: 'Thriving Communities Fund',
        tagline: 'Patient capital for community ownership and land.',
        building: 'The Thriving Communities Fund (TCF) pools charitable capital to provide patient capital for community ownership. We make mostly 0% loans to community organizations acquiring real estate and place-based businesses, with a focus on communities that have been marginalized and shut out of capital, so people can build ownership and stewardship and thrive in place. TCF grew out of a simple observation: hundreds of billions of charitable dollars sit in the capital markets, often for years, waiting to be given away, while community land trusts, resident-owned communities, and other ownership models struggle to find flexible capital on terms that fit. TCF puts that capital to work now, and again as it’s repaid, and invites donors into a peer community rather than a transaction.',
        bring: '20+ years of social justice work spanning direct service, legal advocacy, policy and capital strategy. That work has shown me that wealth is largely shaped by ownership: who owns the land, buildings and businesses that generate value over time. Redlining, discriminatory lending, land loss and disinvestment have locked Black, Indigenous and other communities of color out of that ownership for generations, and today development and gentrification are displacing many of the same communities. Grants and aid can ease the effects of inequality, but ownership gets at its root. When communities own the assets they depend on, they keep the wealth they create and get a real say in their own future.',
        why: 'I believe DAFs can be much more than a parking place for philanthropic dollars. They can be shared, community-centered infrastructure for moving capital where it’s needed most. I’m excited to learn alongside fellow builders who are reimagining what DAFs can do, and to strengthen TCF through that exchange.',
    },
    {
        name: 'Mairi Jane Fox',
        project: 'Women’s investing cohort',
        tagline: 'A pooled DAF where women learn innovative finance by investing together.',
        building: 'A pooled DAF where women learn about innovative finance principles by investing together. Each cohort starts with a shared curriculum that busts the investing jargon. Then we invest real money in companies, using whatever deal structure fits each company’s mission, like revenue-sharing or a structured exit that lets founders buy back ownership instead of selling to the highest bidder. Figuring out what fits is part of the learning. I have two goals. The first is confidence: women control more and more wealth, but most investment education wasn’t designed with us in mind, and practicing real deals together changes that. The second is proof: every deal adds to the track record showing these tools work. People invented this financial system. And we can reinvent it.',
        bring: 'I’ve watched brilliant companies take the wrong capital, drift from their mission, and get bought by the incumbents they set out to challenge. I was a professor of economics and finance, with a PhD in natural resources focused on ecological economics, and ran the business school’s sustainability center. I then became Techstars’ first Director of ESG, joined the leadership team of a climate startup, studied innovative finance at Oxford, was a fellow at the Innovative Finance Initiative, and joined a climate justice fund’s investment committee. Teaching keeps pulling me back: I recently taught innovative finance to MBA students, co-designed a real-money impact investing practicum at the Center for Sustainable Finance and Private Wealth, and now serve on the advisory council for a new rotational training program for impact investors.',
        why: 'I want to pressure-test this model alongside peers doing inspiring work in the DAF space.',
    },
    {
        name: 'Wendy Weiden',
        project: 'A new approach to investing in restaurants',
        tagline: 'Putting DAF dollars to work for Bay Area small businesses.',
        building: 'In the Bay Area, billions of dollars chase the next high-risk startup. Meanwhile, the small business owners who make our neighborhoods worth living in struggle to raise modest amounts of capital. I’m building ways to put DAF dollars to work for them. I’m piloting forgivable, low-interest loans to restaurateurs who meet impact criteria we set together. The first is Ilna, a California-Lebanese restaurant that is deeply personal to its founder, Maz. I’m also developing a multi-donor lending vehicle for a local small-business nonprofit.',
        bring: 'I came to this work through food. After a master’s in sustainable public policy focused on food systems, I worked on strategy and fundraising for local food businesses and social enterprises. An early nonprofit loan fund didn’t get off the ground, but it led me deep into philanthropy. I earned the Chartered Advisor in Philanthropy designation, served on boards and co-founded the Collective Climate Justice Fund, a multi-donor DAF. Asking how to get more of my peers giving led me to Willowseed, my giving coaching practice where I help individuals build their ‘giving muscle’. I know from experience that the more you use it, the more rewarding it gets.',
        why: 'This work is hard to do alone. Community keeps me going and challenges my thinking. I’m looking forward to learning, building and growing with my peers.',
    },
    {
        name: 'Jessy Kate Schingler',
        project: 'Land Commons Fund',
        tagline: 'Financing land into commons stewardship, off the speculative market.',
        building: 'The Land Commons Fund will finance land purchases with land going into commons-oriented stewardship and coming off the speculative market. The Fund will be a standalone charity holding DAFs, and work like a multi-donor alternative to a Real Estate Investment Trust (REIT), with DAF contributors acting a bit like LPs. We will lend and grant rather than take equity, and we will be able to co-invest alongside non-charitable lenders. We will also be able to take on subordinate loans and higher-risk deals when that’s strategic. We will back novel holding structures, such as new types of land trusts, nature easements, purpose trusts and land back arrangements. By drawing on years of lived experience in and with these projects, we will be able to diligence deals that are difficult for traditional finance to understand, creating an option for individuals and family offices to place values-aligned capital and get predictable returns outside of the stock market.',
        bring: 'I’ve spent two decades building community-led real estate and land stewardship projects. Over that time I’ve also designed governance for collaborative, multi-stakeholder arrangements, with a focus on entity structuring and for-purpose governance. I also work on space policy and international frameworks for governing shared resources, including the Moon. I’m currently qualifying as a solicitor in England and Wales.',
        why: 'To work through open questions such as: How do we finance properties that funders also use? Where has this been tried before? What does diligence cost, and what does the financial model look like?',
    },
    {
        name: 'Geo Kane',
        project: 'CapitalizEd',
        tagline: 'Patient, founder-friendly loans for education and workforce companies.',
        building: 'CapitalizEd pools Donor Advised Funds to provide patient, founder-friendly loans to companies in education and workforce with impact as the first bar. Companies can be tackling high-impact problems across the range of human development including early childhood, K12, higher ed, workforce and economic mobility. Funder participants in Fund 1 will be largely exited founders and others who know the sector and can support founders with their knowledge and network as well as dollars.',
        bring: 'I’ve spent my entire career at the intersection of education, technology, and innovation at companies including Apple, Blackboard, Houghton Mifflin, and Pearson. For the past decade, I led venture investing in education companies and funds at Emerson Collective. I’ve seen where venture helps and where it falls short as a tool supporting innovation and impact.',
        why: 'As a DAF holder, I know that too many people have no idea what they can do with their DAFs. We all learn best and take action when we feel informed and inspired and see strong models and examples. As a capital allocator, I know that we need to mobilize more DAF capital to help solve the enormous challenges we face. I believe that DAF Commons is uniquely positioned to make a difference by increasing awareness, developing tools, and building community that will help get more capital flowing for good.',
    },
];
---
<Base title="Get Involved — DAF Commons">
    <div class="page page-involved">
        <section class="community-hero">
            <div class="container">
                <div class="hero-content scroll-animate">
                    <h1 class="huge accent" data-content="involved_hero_heading">Get Involved</h1>
                    <p class="body-large hero-subtitle" data-content="involved_hero_subtitle">Ways to build the DAF Commons with us: join our member cohort, meet our Entrepreneurs in Residence, find us at events, or share your own DAF story.</p>
                    <div class="hero-jump-row">
                        <a href="#membership" class="hero-jump">Member Cohort</a>
                        <span class="hero-jump-sep">·</span>
                        <a href="#eir" class="hero-jump">Entrepreneurs in Residence</a>
                        <span class="hero-jump-sep">·</span>
                        <a href="#events" class="hero-jump">Events</a>
                        <span class="hero-jump-sep">·</span>
                        <a href="#dafluencer" class="hero-jump">Be a DAFluencer</a>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="container">
                <!-- Membership -->
                <div class="involved-block scroll-animate" id="membership">
                    <div class="section-head">
                        <div class="eyebrow-line"><span class="eyebrow-num">01</span><span data-content="involved_member_label">Our community</span></div>
                        <h2 class="large" data-content="involved_member_heading">Member Cohort</h2>
                        <p class="body-large section-sub" data-content="involved_member_sub">An invitation to join the inaugural DAF Commons member cohort</p>
                    </div>
                    <p class="about-body" data-content="involved_member_body">The DAF Commons is a peer community of DAF holders who want to do more with their DAF dollars, together, today. This year we’re inviting ~50 people to form our inaugural cohort. You’ll join us for a roughly six-month founding pilot, starting January 2027, that transitions into ongoing membership. The founding cohort will get support on shifting DAF capital to impact, and help determine how we build the DAF Commons community — how we want to organize, connect, and move from isolated intent to collective action. Broader membership will open later in 2027.</p>
                    <p class="involved-deadline" data-content="involved_member_deadline">Apply by December 4th.</p>
                    <div class="involved-actions">
                        <a class="button btn-outline" data-href="involved_member_learn_url" href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1eF2tZ7g3sHRWXBm3gcK6wQFoKfqFOkFDBQgP0PDWfW0/edit?tab=t.0" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-content="involved_member_learn_label">Learn more about what’s on offer</a>
                        <a class="button btn-primary" data-href="involved_member_apply_url" href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1us412DLaS047VyPLlNC4TkrA25zH8q0ipWscX5H34r8/viewform" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-content="involved_member_apply_label">Apply to join the inaugural cohort</a>
                    </div>
                    <p class="involved-questions">
                        <span data-content="involved_member_questions_1">Questions? Read the</span>
                        <a data-href="involved_member_faq_url" href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1eF2tZ7g3sHRWXBm3gcK6wQFoKfqFOkFDBQgP0PDWfW0/edit?tab=t.0" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-content="involved_member_faq_label">FAQs</a><span data-content="involved_member_questions_2">, join one of our Q&amp;A sessions on</span>
                        <a data-href="involved_member_session_1_url" href="https://luma.com/otygovef" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-content="involved_member_session_1_label">November 17 at 3pm ET / 12pm PT</a>
                        <span data-content="involved_member_questions_3">or</span>
                        <a data-href="involved_member_session_2_url" href="https://luma.com/h94ktoym" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-content="involved_member_session_2_label">November 23 at 1pm ET / 10am PT</a><span data-content="involved_member_questions_4">, or email</span>
                        <a href="mailto:dafcommons@gmail.com" data-content="involved_member_contact_email">dafcommons@gmail.com</a>.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <!-- Entrepreneurs in Residence -->
                <div class="involved-block scroll-animate" id="eir">
                    <div class="section-head">
                        <div class="eyebrow-line"><span class="eyebrow-num">02</span><span data-content="involved_eir_label">Our builders</span></div>
                        <h2 class="large" data-content="involved_eir_heading">Entrepreneurs in Residence</h2>
                        <p class="body-large section-sub" data-content="involved_eir_sub">Meet the inaugural cohort building something new in the world of DAFs</p>
                    </div>
                    <p class="about-body" data-content="involved_eir_body">The Entrepreneurs in Residence (EIR) program gives DAF holders the space, community and support to build something new in the world of DAFs. We started it after meeting DAF holders who, frustrated by the system, were building the pooled funds, initiatives, and products they wished existed, but mostly doing it alone. Over eight months, our EIRs will learn from each other, test concepts, and launch new initiatives, and our community will have chances to engage with them and their work along the way. Our hope is that together they help build a new norm for DAF capital: impact-first investing rather than the traditional “grow to give” model. Meet our inaugural cohort.</p>
                </div>

                <h3 class="medium eir-grid-heading scroll-animate" data-content="involved_eir_action_label">Meet the EIRs</h3>
                <div class="eir-grid" id="eir-cohort">
                    {eirs.map((eir, i) => {
                        const n = i + 1;
                        return (
                            <button type="button" class="eir-card scroll-animate" data-eir-open={`eir-dialog-${n}`} aria-haspopup="dialog">
                                <div class="eir-card-text">
                                    <h3 class="eir-name" data-content={`involved_eir_${n}_name`}>{eir.name}</h3>
                                    <div class="team-role" data-content={`involved_eir_${n}_project`}>{eir.project}</div>
                                    <p class="eir-tagline" data-content={`involved_eir_${n}_tagline`}>{eir.tagline}</p>
                                    <span class="eir-more" data-content="involved_eir_more_label">Read more</span>
                                </div>
                            </button>
                        );
                    })}
                </div>

                {eirs.map((eir, i) => {
                    const n = i + 1;
                    return (
                        <dialog class="eir-dialog" id={`eir-dialog-${n}`} aria-labelledby={`eir-dialog-${n}-name`}>
                            <div class="eir-dialog-inner">
                                <button type="button" class="eir-dialog-close" data-eir-close aria-label="Close">
                                    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><line x1="6" y1="6" x2="18" y2="18"/><line x1="18" y1="6" x2="6" y2="18"/></svg>
                                </button>
                                <div class="eir-dialog-head">
                                    <div>
                                        <h3 class="eir-name" id={`eir-dialog-${n}-name`} data-content={`involved_eir_${n}_name`}>{eir.name}</h3>
                                        <div class="team-role" data-content={`involved_eir_${n}_project`}>{eir.project}</div>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="eir-details">
                                    <div class="eir-detail">
                                        <div class="eir-detail-label" data-content="involved_eir_building_label">What I’m building</div>
                                        <p data-content={`involved_eir_${n}_building`}>{eir.building}</p>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="eir-detail">
                                        <div class="eir-detail-label" data-content="involved_eir_bring_label">What I bring</div>
                                        <p data-content={`involved_eir_${n}_bring`}>{eir.bring}</p>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="eir-detail">
                                        <div class="eir-detail-label" data-content="involved_eir_why_label">Why I’m here</div>
                                        <p data-content={`involved_eir_${n}_why`}>{eir.why}</p>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </dialog>
                    );
                })}

                <!-- Events -->
                <div class="involved-block involved-events" id="events">
                    <div class="section-head scroll-animate">
                        <div class="eyebrow-line"><span class="eyebrow-num">03</span><span data-content="involved_events_label">Events</span></div>
                        <h2 class="large" data-content="involved_events_heading">Find us in person</h2>
                        <p class="body-large section-sub" data-content="involved_events_sub">Find DAF Commons and other DAF holders at events across the world.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="event-list" id="eventList"></div>
                    <p class="event-host-prompt scroll-animate">
                        Hosting something we should be at? <a href="mailto:DAFCommons@gmail.com?subject=Event%20suggestion" class="copy-email-link">Tell us →</a>
                    </p>
                </div>

                <!-- DAFluencer -->
                <div class="involved-block scroll-animate" id="dafluencer">
                    <div class="section-head">
                        <div class="eyebrow-line"><span class="eyebrow-num">04</span><span data-content="involved_dafluencer_label">Share your story</span></div>
                        <h2 class="large" data-content="involved_dafluencer_heading">Be a DAFluencer</h2>
                        <p class="body-large section-sub" data-content="involved_dafluencer_sub">Doing something interesting with your DAF? Inspire other DAF holders by sharing your journey in DAF holders in the wild.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="involved-actions">
                        <a href="/education#stories" class="button btn-primary" data-content="involved_dafluencer_read">Read the stories</a>
                        <a href="mailto:DAFCommons@gmail.com?subject=My%20DAF%20story" class="button btn-outline" data-content="involved_dafluencer_pitch">Pitch your story</a>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>
    </div>
    <script is:inline>
        document.querySelectorAll('[data-eir-open]').forEach(btn => {
            btn.addEventListener('click', function() {
                document.getElementById(this.dataset.eirOpen)?.showModal();
            });
        });
        document.querySelectorAll('.eir-dialog').forEach(dialog => {
            dialog.querySelector('[data-eir-close]')?.addEventListener('click', () => dialog.close());
            // Close when clicking the backdrop (outside the inner panel)
            dialog.addEventListener('click', e => {
                if (e.target === dialog) dialog.close();
            });
        });
    </script>
</Base>
